From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: v2: enable the internal audio codec

The projector's speaker sits on the internal codec, as on the bench
board (0082). The V2 tree left codec@2030000 disabled, so ALSA had no
card, PipeWire had no sink, and the HDMI speaker service could not
start. Enable it. A RAM copy of the V2 tree with only this change
registered "H713 Audio Codec" and passed the speaker playback and pop
tests on the projector (2026-11-21).

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2.dts
@@ -98,6 +98,9 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* The speaker is on the internal codec (bench board: 0082). */
+&codec { status = "okay"; };
+
 /* The HDMI receiver and capture drivers own these from the boot handoff. */
 &audio_bridge { status = "disabled"; };
 &tvtop { status = "disabled"; };
